# AI Reconciliation Engine - Cursor Rules

## Project Context
Financial reconciliation tool. Next.js 14 App Router + TypeScript + Tailwind + OpenAI API.
Users upload 2 CSVs (bank statement + ledger), AI matches transactions, humans review uncertain matches, export report.

## Code Style
- TypeScript strict mode. No `any` types — define interfaces in lib/types.ts
- Functional components only. No class components.
- Use server components by default. Add "use client" only when needed (interactivity, useState, event handlers).
- API routes in app/api/ using Route Handlers (export async function POST/GET)
- Use async/await, never .then() chains
- Error handling: try/catch in API routes, return NextResponse.json with proper status codes
- File naming: kebab-case for files, PascalCase for components

## Architecture Rules
- All OpenAI calls happen server-side in API routes. Never expose API keys to client.
- Matching logic lives in lib/matcher.ts — pure functions, no side effects, fully testable.
- Components are presentational. Data fetching happens via fetch() to API routes.
- No database. All state lives in React state during the session. This is an MVP.
- No external state management library. useState and useReducer are sufficient.

## UI/Design Rules
- Tailwind CSS only. No CSS modules, no styled-components.
- Dark theme: bg-slate-950, bg-slate-900 for cards, text-slate-100 for primary text
- Accent colors: sky-400 (primary), emerald-500 (success/matched), amber-500 (review), red-500 (unmatched)
- Confidence badges: green (>90%), amber (70-90%), red (<70%)
- Tables must be responsive. Use overflow-x-auto wrapper.
- All amounts display with PKR currency format and thousand separators.

## OpenAI Integration
- Model: gpt-4o-mini (fast + cheap for batch comparisons)
- Send transaction pairs in batches of 10-20 to minimize API calls
- Prompt should return JSON with confidence score (0-100) and match reasoning
- Temperature: 0 (deterministic for financial data)
- Always include a system prompt explaining the reconciliation context

## CSV Data Format Expected
Bank statement columns: Date, Description, Debit, Credit, Balance, Reference
Ledger columns: Date, Description, Amount, Type (debit/credit), Reference, Invoice_No

## Posting & Missing Entries
- `lib/entries.ts` — generate missing ledger/bank lines from unmatched rows; post matched pairs to journal log
- `POST /api/generate-missing` — returns proposals for bank-only and ledger-only unmatched items
- `POST /api/post-entries` — posts matchIds (auto_matched/approved) and/or proposalIds (generated entries)
- Posted matches use status `posted`; generated entries use matchType `generated`
- MVP: no ERP integration — posts are session journal log + CSV export audit trail

## Testing
- Test matching logic with known inputs/outputs
- Include edge cases: partial amounts, date offsets, name variations, duplicates
- Sample data in /data folder for manual testing

## Git
- Never commit .env.local or any file containing API keys
- .env.example must list all required vars with placeholder values
- Meaningful commit messages: "feat: add fuzzy matching engine" not "update"
